@startuml
title BoomDB — simplified UML component diagram
skinparam componentStyle uml2
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam defaultFontSize 16
skinparam defaultFontColor #182126
skinparam defaultTextAlignment center
skinparam titleFontSize 25
skinparam titleFontStyle bold
skinparam stereotypeFontSize 14
skinparam componentBackgroundColor white
skinparam componentBorderColor #263238
skinparam artifactBackgroundColor white
skinparam artifactBorderColor #263238
skinparam arrowColor #263238
skinparam arrowFontSize 15
skinparam arrowFontColor #182126
skinparam nodesep 100
skinparam ranksep 100
top to bottom direction

' Group existing classes by responsibility to keep the architecture readable.
component "<size:22><b>SQL front end</b></size>\n\nEngine · Executor\nSqlParser · SqlAstBuilder · Binder" as Front <<component>>
component "<size:22><b>Query execution</b></size>\n\nPlanner\nScanOperator · FilterOperator" as Query <<component>>
component "<size:22><b>Storage</b></size>\n\nStorageEngine · StorageSupport" as Storage <<component>>
component "<size:22><b>Catalog</b></size>\n\nCatalogStore\nSchema · partitions · min/max" as Catalog <<component>>
artifact "catalogs/<table>.json" as CatalogFile <<artifact>>
artifact "data/<table>-<partition>.bin\n<size:15>PAX binary partitions</size>" as Partitions <<artifact>>

' UML dependencies point from the component using a service to its supplier.
Front .right.> Query : plan and execute\nSELECT
Front ..> Storage : CREATE / COPY\nschema lookup
Query .down.> Storage : metadata lookup\npartition reads
Storage .left.> Catalog : load / save\nmetadata
Catalog .down.> CatalogFile : read / write
Storage .down.> Partitions : read / write

' Invisible constraints keep the SVG's two columns and three rows:
' Front / Query, Catalog / Storage, then their respective file artifacts.
Front -[hidden]down- Catalog
CatalogFile -[hidden]right- Partitions

skinparam footerFontSize 14
center footer
  Dashed open arrows = uses dependencies. All four components run in one Java process.
  File paths are relative to the configured database root.
endfooter
@enduml
